    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0547" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.00/595: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1919-04-12T07:05:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1919-04-07T00:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April
                            12, 1919, 7.05 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from Consul General [at] Seoul April 11, 5 p.m. Yesterday gendarmes
                    entered Severance Hospital, American institution, and took to police station
                    under protest of surgeon, three Korean patients suffering from serious gunshot
                    wounds inflicted by police. Superintendent general police assured Curtice who
                    demanded explanation, that action was strictly according to law as men were
                    criminals. Report follows.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d415-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
